WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.912
Today’s lesson goal: Today’s lesson goal: turn vague asks into clear prompts. Separate role, task, constraints, and format. Test outputs before you trust them.

2
00:00:13.762 --> 00:00:26.794
The prompt recipe: Use a prompt recipe. Role: who the model should act as. Goal: what success looks like. Add constraints and an output shape you can check.

3
00:00:27.644 --> 00:00:44.372
Vague vs specific: Compare vague versus specific. Vague says summarise this meeting. Specific asks for actions, owners, and deadlines as a J S O N list. Specific prompts fail loudly — that is useful.

4
00:00:45.222 --> 00:00:57.006
Worked rewrite: Worked rewrite: add role project assistant. Require only using the notes provided. Return bullets in the shape action, owner, date.

5
00:00:57.856 --> 00:01:09.352
Few-shot when it helps: Use a few-shot example when it helps. Show one short correct example close to your real format. Remove examples that teach the wrong pattern.

6
00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:25.730
Test before you trust: Test before you trust. Try good, empty, and conflicting inputs. Score format, factuality, and helpfulness. Tighten the rules, then retest the same cases.

7
00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:39.132
Practice checkpoint: Practice checkpoint: rewrite one vague request from your day. Save the before and after in the starter pack. Then continue in the written Prompting Basics lesson.
